    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n10965" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">con-vāso</span></b> , āvi,
			ātum, 1, v. a.
		vasa, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>to pack vessels</i> or <i>implements together, to
				pack up</i> (the figure taken from milit. lang.; anteand
			post-class. and very rare). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: aliquid convasassem, * <i><span class="en">Ter. Phorm.
				1, 4, 13</span></i>; so <i><span class="en">Sid. Ep. 7,
			2</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">acclamationes,</span>”
				<i>to pile up</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Sid. Ep. 1, 9 <i>fin.</i></span></i>
			</div>
